  "notes": "Run diagnostics is now directly under Connection and in Settings. Customers can check USB detection, fresh droid replies, reported screen health, repeated reconnects, display settings, playlist state and online-data availability. Results include clear codes and next steps, even when no droid is found.\n\nA temporary eight-second checkerboard tests screen visibility through the existing live-display protocol. It does not install firmware or change saved settings. Customers can record whether the pattern was visible, review a local support report and save it to send to DroidFun support. Reports include the droid hardware ID for Workshop identification and exclude credentials, account details, custom text/images and local paths. Nothing is sent automatically.\n\nVerified compatible standard legacy boards retain manual 1.2.4 recovery with a fresh native preflight. Factory, newer, custom, unidentified and swapped-wiring boards are protected from generic reinstalls. Firmware is unchanged. Existing custom text, scrolling and image screens remain available.\n",
